SwiftCrossUI's WinUI backend, two changes to propose upstream:

1. Split view: the pane kept being reset to the sidebar's minimum width on every layout, and the
   relayout hook was internal, so an app could neither size the sidebar nor slide it. The width is
   now clamped to the bounds instead (as AppKit's divider is), and CustomSplitView's hook is public.

2. Text measurement cache: each measurement went through XAML (a dozen calls and a layout pass);
   layouts measure the same strings at the same sizes on every frame of a resize. Cleared when the
   system text scaling changes.
